      "body": "## Motivation\n\nKDA models with a bounded safe gate (for example, Kimi-K3 with `gate_lower_bound=-5.0`) fail when dispatched to FlashInfer decode or target verification. The dispatcher rejects every non-Triton kernel, although FlashInfer already forwards `lower_bound` to `recurrent_kda`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Declare `supports_safe_gate=True` on the linear attention kernel base; CuTe DSL retains its explicit False override.\n- Select effective decode and verify kernels by safe-gate capability, matching the existing extend fallback. Keep FlashInfer selected and reroute unsupported kernels to Triton.\n- Read the declared capability directly in the extend selector.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Isolated execution of the dispatcher source with mocked kernels: 18 cases covering decode, verify, and extend, supported/unsupported safe gate, and bounds None, -5.0, and 0.0. Confirmed original decode/verify rejection and fixed selection, lower_bound forwarding, and absence of calls to the other backend.\n- Repository pre-commit checks passed on both changed files; the branch-name guard was excluded. `git diff --check` passed.\n- This checkout has no PyTorch, Triton, or GPU; full kernel and model tests were not run here. The isolated checks are not committed CI tests.\n- Reporter-provided validation with this fix AND the separate prefill tuple-unpacking fix: Kimi-K3 with `--linear-attn-prefill-backend flashkda --linear-attn-decode-backend flashinfer`, 356-token health-check prefill returned HTTP 200, 120-token generation completed, and no traceback was observed. This is combined functional validation, not an accuracy benchmark or a standalone validation of this commit.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run. Kernel computations are unchanged; this fixes Python backend dispatch.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format and lint checks passed.\n- [ ] Add registered CI regression tests.\n- [x] No new user-facing options or documentation changes required.\n- [ ] Full model accuracy and speed benchmarks.\n- [x] Follow existing code style.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35995135360](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35995135360)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35995134944](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35995134944)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35995135393](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35995135393)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
